-- CK-254: a parameter's folded levels are not checked (paramHole, issue #286).
-- ownership-checker.md §16.7, the open item "A parameter's folded levels are
-- not yet checked". `hole` takes a tree, pushes onto its root's list and
-- returns its left subtree beside it. The symbolic cell of the left subtree,
-- `param(t, #Node.0)`, does not cover `param(t, #Node.1)`, the lists of every
-- level, so the push is accepted `param` on master. `shared` hands it a tree
-- that holds `xs` at two levels, so in place the subtree it returns sees the
-- push. The same body over a tree built inline is rejected (`FoldLevels`).
-- The expected golden is written by reasoning, before the fix: the push is
-- rejected `element` because the left subtree may hold the root's list, as
-- the inline twin is. Decision (d) of §16.7 (`lvl`) would instead accept the
-- push with `xreq lvl π1` and reject `shared`'s call; whoever builds (d)
-- blesses the real lines and checks that `shared` is refused.
type Tree
    = Leaf
    | Node Tree (List Int) Tree


pub hole : Tree → List Int × Tree
hole t =
    case t of
        Node l ys _ →
            ( List.push ys 1, l )

        Leaf →
            ( [], Leaf )


pub shared : List Int → List Int × Tree
shared xs = hole (Node (Node Leaf xs Leaf) xs Leaf)
